.TH ASTRAL-GUARD 1 "2026-08-15" "astral-hwmon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
astral\-guard \- check the 12VHPWR connector of an ASUS ROG Astral card
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B astral\-guard
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the per\-pin voltages and currents published by the
.B astral\-hwmon
driver, samples them a few times, applies a fixed set of connector rules and
exits with a monitoring\-plugin status code.
.PP
It requires no configuration, no calibration and no privileges: every attribute
it reads is world\-readable, and all of them are opened read\-only. It never
writes anything.
.PP
A finding is reported only if it holds in every sample of a run. This is
deliberate: the vendor's own tool is documented to report spurious 0 A and
over\-current readings immediately after resume from sleep, and a single\-sample
verdict would inherit that.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable output, including the thresholds that were applied.
.TP
.BI \-\-samples " N"
Samples per run. Default 5.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " MS"
Milliseconds between samples. Defaults to the chip's own
.IR update_interval .
Sampling faster than that only re\-reads the driver's cache.
.TP
.BI \-\-sysfs\-root " PATH"
Where sysfs is mounted. Defaults to
.IR /sys .
.TP
.BI \-\-warn\-ratio " PCT"
The min/max warning threshold, as a percentage. Provisional \- see LIMITATIONS.
.TP
.BI \-\-note\-ratio " PCT"
The min/max advisory threshold. Advisory findings are printed but never change
the exit code.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Print only when the result is not OK. Useful from
.BR cron (8),
which then mails only on a problem.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH RULES
.TP
.B pin\-current
WARNING at 9.2 A on any pin, CRITICAL at 9.5 A. Never gated.
.TP
.B open\-pin
CRITICAL when a pin carries under 0.5 A while the connector as a whole draws at
least 10 A. A pin that has stopped conducting pushes its share onto its
neighbours.
.TP
.B imbalance
The ratio of the least\-loaded to the most\-loaded pin, evaluated only above 20 A
total. Advisory below 85%, WARNING below 70%, CRITICAL below 60%.
.TP
.B voltage
WARNING when the lowest pin falls below 11.4 V, CRITICAL below 11.0 V.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
OK.
.TP
.B 1
WARNING.
.TP
.B 2
CRITICAL.
.TP
.B 3
UNKNOWN \- no chip found, or a channel could not be read. Losing sight of the
current is a fault, not silence.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Absolute rules only. Without a per\-card baseline this catches a connector that
is already near failure, not one drifting toward it.
.PP
Current is a proxy for the contact heating that actually melts connectors. A
green result is not a temperature claim.
.PP
The warning threshold for imbalance is provisional. It is set at a value one
commercial monitor abandoned as too noisy, kept as a warning rather than an
alarm for that reason, and is expected to move as more cards are measured.
.PP
Resume behaviour has been measured on one machine and for S3 sleep only: no
spurious reading appeared, reads during the window failed rather than
returning a decodable frame, and the verdict was OK within a tenth of a second
of wake. Hibernate and s2idle are untested, as is every card but one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/class/hwmon/hwmon*/
Located by the
.I name
attribute, never by index.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sensors (1)
